course: dictionary
lesson: 13314
title: Grime
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Grime is dirt that has built up into a thick, sticky or black layer on a surface or on your skin. It does not come off with a quick wipe.
explain: «The grime on the windows made the room dark.» The clues are windows and dark. Grime is dirt that stops light getting through, so it must be a thick layer of dirt.
explain: Grime can also mean a style of fast rap music that started in London around 2002. Look at the words around it to tell which meaning is meant: «The grime track blasted from the car speakers» is about music, not dirt.
fact: Grime (noun) means dirt that has built up in a thick, sticky or black layer.
fact: «Grimy» is the adjective: «The grimy kitchen needed a good scrub.»
fact: «After mending my bike, my hands were covered in black grime.»
fact: Grime is an uncountable noun, so we say some grime, not a grime.
fact: Grime is also a fast style of rap music that started in London around 2002.
exercise: «The grime on the windows made the room dark.» What is the grime? | *Thick dirt that has built up on the glass | A kind of window frame | A bright light shining through the glass | A cleaning spray
exercise: «After mending my bike, my hands were covered in black grime.» Which word is the adjective for grime? | grinning | grime | *grimy | gritty
exercise: Grime is also a style of music. Where did it start? | Dublin | Glasgow | Sydney | *London
test: «The old factory walls were covered in grime from years of smoke.» What does grime mean here? | *Thick black dirt | Fresh air | A kind of brick | Bright paint
test: Which sentence uses grimy correctly? | The grimy sunshine warmed the garden. | The grimy song made everyone smile. | The grimy birthday cake was sweet. | *The grimy pan needed a long scrub.
exam: «Soot and grime covered the city streets.» What clue tells you grime means dirt? | The city, which is big | *Soot, which is black dirt from smoke | The children, who are happy | The streets, which are long
